# Generated SSR/client chunk cache that USED to land in the REPO ROOT under a
# random nanoid-style directory (`<id>/client/`, `<id>/ssr/`, hashed filenames
# containing __vite_ssr_exports__), swept in by `git add -A` three times
# (#879, #1003).
#
# THE REAL FIX IS NOT HERE: apps/web/vitest.config.ts now pins `cacheDir` to an
# absolute path under node_modules, so the cache cannot reach the repo root
# regardless of the nanoid or the cwd vitest runs from. This list is a belt-and
# -braces leftover, kept because a stale checkout may still have these on disk.
#
# It was never sufficient on its own, and failed in BOTH directions: a random
# name cannot be matched generically (gitignore has no regex quantifiers), and
# listing one here never untracked it — BgslqnjILApu8jL_vIFuC was listed AND
# still committed until #1005. Prefer the cacheDir pin plus the top-level
# directory guard in .github/workflows over adding a fourth entry here.
/sco5yHj4dsqv45Yc8yrM5/
/BgslqnjILApu8jL_vIFuC/
/t19GkuBguxG71m2b6fymV/
